-- title:
--   Generic étaleness of j-fibres on the level-p modular curve
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Write $F$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the intermediate field of the field of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,j_q$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $p$, and let $j =$ `IgusaScheme.jFull p` be the element $j_q$ of $F$. Let $A =$ `Afin p` be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra `chartAlg ℤ F {j}` of $F$, the finite-$j$ chart ring of the two-chart integral model, and let `jChartFin` be $j$ regarded as an element of $A$. The assertion is that there exists a nonzero $c_0 \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with the following property: for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose image in $\mathbb{Q}[X]$ is irreducible and which does not divide $c_0$ in $\mathbb{Z}[X]$, the quotient of $\mathbb{Q} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} A$ by the ideal generated by the single element $1 \otimes g(j)$ (evaluation of $g$ at `jChartFin` inside $A$) is an étale $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra.
--
--   This is the statement that the level set $\{g(j)=0\}$ on the affine modular curve of level $p$ is étale over $\mathbb{Q}$ as soon as the irreducible monic $g$ avoids a fixed finite set of critical values of $j$, encoded by divisibility of $c_0$. It feeds the construction of finite étale algebras attached to $j$-fibres in [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin).
